 Install Git

Step 1: Configure Git (First Time Only)
>>> git config --global user.name "Your Name"
>>> git config --global user.email "your_email@example.com"

Verify:

>>> git config --list
.................................

Step 2: Create a Project Folder

Step 3: Initialize Git Repository
  git init

Step 4: Check Repository Status
 git status

Step 5: Add Files
 
 git add .

Step 6: Commit Changes
 git commit -m "Initial project setup"
 

Step 7: Create a New Branch
 git branch feature-csv-json

Check branches:
 git branch
 
Step 8: Commit Changes

 Check status:
 git status
 Add changes:
 git add task1.py

Commit:
 git commit -m "Completed CSV and JSON practice"
.................................................

Step 9: Create GitHub Repository
 Go to GitHub.
 Create a repository named:
 Week2-Python
 Do not initialize it with a README if your local project already has one.

Step 10: Connect Local Repository to GitHub

 Replace <username> with your GitHub username.
 git remote add origin https://github.com/<syedmehdishah05>/Week2-Python.git

Verify:

 git remote -v

Step 11: Push Code

 Push the main branch:
 git push -u origin main
 Push the feature branch:
 
Step 12: Create a Pull Request

 On GitHub:
 Open your repository.
 Click Compare & pull request.
 Add a title.

Example:

 Completed CSV & JSON Task
 Description:
 Added Task 1 solution.
 Implemented CSV and JSON reading, writing, parsing, and filtering.

Click:

 Create Pull Request


Step 13: Merge Pull Request
 Click:
 Merge Pull Request
 Then:
 Confirm Merge
 
Step 14: Update Local Main Branch
 Switch back:
 git switch main
 Pull latest changes:
 git pull origin main


Step 15: Delete Feature Branch
 Delete locally:
 git branch -d feature-csv-json
 Delete on GitHub:
 git push origin --delete feature-csv-json

........................................

